    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Structural pattern</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 2</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Adapter</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Plug a payment SDK, a legacy library or a C API into the interface your code already uses, without touching either side. Learn object vs class adapters, what an adapter should and should not do, and how to tell it apart from Facade, Decorator and Proxy in one sentence each.</p>\r\n"
